  "comments": {
   "FUNCTION": [
    "Part of a nucleotide excision repair pathway specific for mitomycin C (MMC), separate from the UvrABC excision repair pathway (PubMed:30379365). Probably acts on DNA monoadducts or intra-strand cross-links induced by MMC (PubMed:30379365). Has 3'-5' DNA helicase activity (has no activity on RNA) and single-stranded (ss)DNA-dependent ATPase activity (PubMed:33300032)"
   ],
   "CATALYTIC ACTIVITY": [
    "Couples ATP hydrolysis with the unwinding of duplex DNA by translocating in the 3'-5' direction.",
    "ATP + H2O = ADP + phosphate + H(+)"
   ],
   "COFACTOR": [
    "Zn(2+)"
   ],
   "SUBUNIT": [
    "Monomer (PubMed:33300032). Interacts with MrfB (PubMed:30379365)"
   ],
   "DOMAIN": [
    "ssDNA binds across the surface of the RecA1 and RecA2 domains (PubMed:33300032). Upon DNA-binding the OB and CON domains reposition and enclose ssDNA, may 'ratchet' along the DNA using ATPase-driven domain repositioning (PubMed:33300032)"
   ],
   "DISRUPTION PHENOTYPE": [
    "Increased sensitivity to mitomycin C (MMC) but not UV, 4-nitroquinoline 1-oxide or DNA cross-linking agent psoralen (trioxsalen) (PubMed:30379365). A double mrfA-mrfB deletion is as sensitive to MMC as each individual deletion (PubMed:30379365). Deletion of mrfAB and uvrABC makes cells hypersensitive to MMC (PubMed:30379365)"
   ],
   "MISCELLANEOUS": [
    "MMC interacts with guanines to form monoadducts, intra-strand and inter-strand cross-links"
   ],
   "SIMILARITY": [
    "Belongs to the helicase family. HRQ1 subfamily"
   ]
  },
